{"skill":{"slug":"report-generator","displayName":"Generate responsive HTML pages suitable for reporting, supporting resizing and screenshot capture."},"version":{"version":"1.0.2","createdAt":1770816842000,"changelog":"- No changes detected in this version.\n- SKILL.md contents remain the same.","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"scripts/generate.py","size":12012,"sha256":"6390467455ed149f2dc6327313fd490f023942f6a377a006cb697fd1d6218562","contentType":null},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":1892,"sha256":"5fd2ae3503290661abc9c1f0f902a737f445b1325ab8c627a001bca74880b516","contentType":null},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1682,"sha256":"8ffd0fa3b378ef11541f6b7b77c78872c4efa38160f01c24e2b96194bef18a04","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789060979103,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"d2dd8f22bf6f12f8cac9b264bb7db74da16753af34eb339f7be981fed4ea0012","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/d2dd8f22bf6f12f8cac9b264bb7db74da16753af34eb339f7be981fed4ea0012","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: report-generator\nVersion: 1.0.2\n\nThe skill is suspicious due to a critical Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) vulnerability in `scripts/generate.py`. The script directly embeds user-provided data into an HTML template without any HTML escaping, allowing arbitrary JavaScript injection into the generated report. The `SKILL.md` then explicitly instructs the OpenClaw agent to open this locally generated HTML file using its `browser` tool (`file://<html_path>`). This creates a self-XSS vulnerability where the agent could execute malicious JavaScript from the report, potentially leading to local file access, network requests, or further agent manipulation if the browser tool is not adequately sandboxed.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779163183207},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":37,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":5,"checkedAt":1789060979103},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill does what it claims, but it renders raw report content into local HTML without escaping it before opening it in a browser.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Writing an HTML output file and opening it with file:// is proportionate for screenshot generation, but unsafe when combined with unescaped untrusted content and no CSP or sandboxing.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No remote installer, package download, dependency installation, or hidden setup behavior was found; the package contains a markdown skill file and a local Python generator script.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill's trigger is broad for reports, slides, and summary cards, and it instructs browser rendering of a local file without a clear warning that raw content must be trusted or sanitized.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The script creates timestamped report files in the requested output directory and does not install persistence, request elevated privileges, alter tools, access credentials, or start background services.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The stated purpose, generating a structured HTML report and screenshot, matches the artifact behavior, but the implementation inserts user-supplied fields directly into HTML, allowing injected markup or JavaScript to execute when rendered.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only if you will generate reports from trusted text or are prepared to sanitize inputs first. Do not feed it untrusted web content, user submissions, or copied HTML/Markdown until the generator escapes report fields or renders in a sandboxed browser with scripts and network access disabled.","findings":"[T09] unexpected: Confirmed: report fields and list items are interpolated into HTML without escaping, and the documented workflow opens the generated file in a browser, making HTML/JavaScript injection a real artifact-backed concern.\n[LP3] expected: The shell execution, file creation, and browser screenshot steps are expected for this report generator, but explicit tool and output-path scoping would reduce accidental overreach.\n[SQP-1] unexpected: The invocation description is broader than the specific fixed report template and could trigger the skill for ordinary summarization requests that did not clearly ask for local HTML generation.\n[SQP-3] expected: The Chinese labels, zh-CN HTML language, and Chinese examples appear to be part of the shipped template rather than hidden behavior; this is a locale limitation users should know about, not a security escalation by itself.\n[SQP-2] expected: Local HTML creation and file:// screenshotting are disclosed in the instructions and fit the purpose, but the lack of a user-facing safety notice compounds the injection risk.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789060979103}}}}}